WEBVTT

00:00:56.956 --> 00:01:00.687
To any vessels within range,
I hope this message reaches you.

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:04.629
I'm an HD-25
isomorphic projection.

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:06.461
There's been an accident.

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:07.966
My crew is dead.

00:01:08.001 --> 00:01:09.434
I'm alone.

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:14.496
Please, help me.

00:03:10.788 --> 00:03:13.188
So we rigged
the security console,

00:03:13.224 --> 00:03:17.126
so that every time Tuvok
accessed the internal sensors,

00:03:17.161 --> 00:03:18.355
it would play
a little message...

00:03:18.396 --> 00:03:21.263
"Live long and prosper."

00:03:21.298 --> 00:03:23.266
No matter what button
he pushed:

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:24.562
"Live long and prosper."

00:03:24.602 --> 00:03:26.433
Naturally, no one
was available

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:27.960
to fix the malfunction, so...

00:03:28.072 --> 00:03:30.870
So Tuvok had to stretch
his Vulcan patience to the limit

00:03:30.908 --> 00:03:32.136
for the rest of the day.

00:03:32.176 --> 00:03:34.542
I swear you could hear
him grinding his teeth

00:03:34.578 --> 00:03:35.806
from across the Bridge.

00:03:37.682 --> 00:03:38.979
Just when he thought
it was over,

00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:40.950
when he went back
to his quarters,

00:03:40.985 --> 00:03:42.680
and ordered a cup
of Vulcan tea,

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:44.210
the replicator says...

00:03:44.255 --> 00:03:46.450
"Live long and prosper!"

00:03:48.659 --> 00:03:50.388
The first time I met Tuvok,

00:03:50.428 --> 00:03:54.421
he dressed me down in front
of three Starfleet Admirals

00:03:54.465 --> 00:03:57.992
for failing to observe
proper tactical procedures

00:03:58.069 --> 00:03:59.832
during my first command.

00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:02.930
My human ego took
a little bruising, but...

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:04.837
of course, he was right.

00:04:06.243 --> 00:04:10.907
Over the past nine years,
I've come to rely

00:04:10.948 --> 00:04:16.477
on his insightful
and unfailingly logical advice.

00:04:17.755 --> 00:04:19.655
For outstanding service

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:22.318
as Chief Tactical
and Security Officer,

00:04:22.359 --> 00:04:24.953
it's my pleasure
to grant you the rank

00:04:25.029 --> 00:04:27.397
of Lieutenant Commander.

00:04:31.934 --> 00:04:34.266
Congratulations, Tuvok.

00:04:34.303 --> 00:04:35.930
Thank you, Captain.

00:04:35.972 --> 00:04:37.837
Had I known this commendation

00:04:37.874 --> 00:04:41.241
entailed ritual humiliation,
I might have declined.

00:04:41.277 --> 00:04:44.735
However, I accept
it with gratitude

00:04:44.781 --> 00:04:46.408
and will honor
the responsibility

00:04:46.449 --> 00:04:47.416
that comes with it.

00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:49.247
During my three years
on Voyager,

00:04:49.285 --> 00:04:51.753
I have grown to respect
a great many of you.

00:04:51.788 --> 00:04:54.450
Others, I have learned
to tolerate.

00:04:54.490 --> 00:04:56.185
As your Tactical Officer,

00:04:56.225 --> 00:04:59.991
I will continue to do my best
to ensure a safe passage home.

00:05:00.096 --> 00:05:03.930
As a Vulcan, I share
the following sentiment:

00:05:05.601 --> 00:05:08.069
Live long and prosper.

00:05:10.039 --> 00:05:11.939
Bravo! Well-deserved.

00:05:16.746 --> 00:05:18.145
B'Elanna.

00:05:22.118 --> 00:05:23.278
This is ridiculous.

00:05:23.319 --> 00:05:24.286
It's been three days,

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:25.685
and we haven't said
a word to each other.

00:05:25.721 --> 00:05:27.518
I know, I know.
We have to talk.

00:05:27.557 --> 00:05:31.323
About what you said,
I mean...

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:34.329
the part about
being in love with me.

00:05:34.363 --> 00:05:37.196
I realize you were suffering
from oxygen deprivation,

00:05:37.233 --> 00:05:40.964
and we were literally
seconds away from death,

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:43.163
so I know you probably
didn't mean it.

00:05:43.206 --> 00:05:45.401
Oh, no, no.
I meant it.

00:05:45.441 --> 00:05:49.969
But I don't expect you
to reciprocate, really.

00:05:50.046 --> 00:05:52.173
Uh, you can just pretend
that I didn't say it.

00:05:52.215 --> 00:05:53.682
In fact, let's just forget
that I even said anything.

00:05:53.716 --> 00:05:54.978
- Shut up.
- I really...

00:06:00.089 --> 00:06:01.886
Mr. Paris, there you are.

00:06:01.924 --> 00:06:03.448
I was just leaving.

00:06:03.493 --> 00:06:04.482
Lieutenant.

00:06:06.162 --> 00:06:07.754
What can I do for you, Doc?

00:06:07.797 --> 00:06:09.162
The Captain
has authorized me

00:06:09.198 --> 00:06:11.564
to recruit someone with
advanced medical training

00:06:11.601 --> 00:06:12.932
to help out in Sick Bay.

00:06:13.035 --> 00:06:16.402
Unfortunately, the most
qualified crew member is you.

00:06:16.439 --> 00:06:17.929
You want me to be
the new nurse?

00:06:18.007 --> 00:06:20.237
If that's the title
you prefer.

00:06:20.276 --> 00:06:21.903
It will only be temporary...

00:06:21.944 --> 00:06:23.411
three duty shifts a week.

00:06:23.446 --> 00:06:25.311
Report to Sick Bay
at 0600 hours.

00:06:25.348 --> 00:06:27.578
Bring a tricorder and a smile.

00:06:27.617 --> 00:06:28.777
What kind of modifications?

00:06:28.818 --> 00:06:30.649
We'd like to enhance
the Astrometrics Lab.

00:06:30.686 --> 00:06:33.655
It hasn't been upgraded
since Voyager left Spacedock.

00:06:33.689 --> 00:06:34.815
I'll start right away.

00:06:34.857 --> 00:06:36.586
I've assigned Seven of Nine
to work with you.

00:06:36.626 --> 00:06:37.752
She's agreed to provide us

00:06:37.793 --> 00:06:39.761
with all the navigational
data for this area

00:06:39.795 --> 00:06:42.229
she acquired during her time
with the Borg.

00:06:42.265 --> 00:06:43.493
Is there a problem?

00:06:43.533 --> 00:06:46.127
No. No problem.

00:06:46.168 --> 00:06:47.635
Try to make her feel
like part of the team.

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:49.194
Right.
Part of the team.

00:06:49.238 --> 00:06:50.466
Have you made arrangements

00:06:50.506 --> 00:06:51.666
with the Arritheans
for tomorrow?

00:06:51.707 --> 00:06:53.436
The delegate says
he's looking forward

00:06:53.476 --> 00:06:55.410
to trading
with such an advanced starship.

00:06:55.444 --> 00:06:56.604
You have done an excellent job

00:06:56.646 --> 00:06:57.977
preparing for this mission,
Neelix.

00:06:58.080 --> 00:06:59.172
I think we should consider this

00:06:59.215 --> 00:07:01.149
your first official assignment
as Ambassador.

00:07:01.183 --> 00:07:02.810
Ensign Culhane to the Captain.

00:07:02.852 --> 00:07:03.910
Janeway here.

00:07:03.986 --> 00:07:05.886
We are receiving
an automated distress call

00:07:05.922 --> 00:07:07.753
five light-years from here.

00:07:07.790 --> 00:07:09.451
You might want
to bring the Doctor.

00:07:13.229 --> 00:07:15.925
I'm an HD-25
isomorphic projection.

00:07:15.965 --> 00:07:18.229
There's been an accident.

00:07:18.267 --> 00:07:19.734
My crew is dead.

00:07:19.769 --> 00:07:21.066
I'm alone.

00:07:23.506 --> 00:07:26.907
Please, help me.

00:07:26.943 --> 00:07:28.308
He's a hologram.

00:07:28.344 --> 00:07:30.312
We've got to help him.

00:07:30.346 --> 00:07:32.541
Ensign, track the source
of the transmission.

00:07:32.582 --> 00:07:35.642
Once we find his ship,
I'll lead an away team.

00:07:35.685 --> 00:07:38.552
I don't recall giving you
a promotion today.

00:07:38.588 --> 00:07:40.613
Oh... well,
I'm the obvious choice

00:07:40.656 --> 00:07:43.386
to provide assistance
to a holographic being.

00:07:43.426 --> 00:07:45.860
Doctor, I don't want you
leaving Voyager

00:07:45.895 --> 00:07:47.886
unless it's
absolutely necessary.

00:07:47.930 --> 00:07:51.331
I'm still concerned about
damaging your mobile emitter.

00:07:51.367 --> 00:07:53.301
I understand.

00:07:53.336 --> 00:07:54.963
But if this is a hologram...

00:07:55.004 --> 00:07:57.063
one of my own kind,
so to speak...

00:07:57.106 --> 00:07:59.597
I'd like to meet him,
study him.

00:07:59.642 --> 00:08:01.371
I'll bring Lieutenant Torres,
just to be safe.

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:03.105
She knows more about my emitter
than anyone.

00:08:04.780 --> 00:08:08.238
The rest of us will meet
with the Arritheans.

00:08:08.284 --> 00:08:11.481
We'll see you there
when you're finished.

00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:14.421
Thank you, Captain.

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:33.704
Seven?

00:08:33.743 --> 00:08:35.404
I am here.

00:08:38.347 --> 00:08:39.905
Am I to work with you?

00:08:39.949 --> 00:08:42.349
Oh, hi. Yes.

00:08:42.385 --> 00:08:44.785
Uh, I thought we'd start
in Jefferies tube 32-B

00:08:44.820 --> 00:08:47.618
enhance
the astrometric sensors...

00:08:47.657 --> 00:08:48.715
if that's okay with you.

00:08:48.758 --> 00:08:49.952
Unless this is a bad time.

00:08:49.992 --> 00:08:51.289
Maybe I can come back later.

00:08:51.327 --> 00:08:54.660
Ensign Kim, you seem...
apprehensive.

00:08:54.697 --> 00:08:57.325
No, not at all.

00:08:57.366 --> 00:08:58.663
The last time
we worked together,

00:08:58.701 --> 00:09:00.225
I struck you at the base
of your skull

00:09:00.269 --> 00:09:01.896
and attempted
to contact the collective.

00:09:01.937 --> 00:09:03.837
These things happen.

00:09:03.873 --> 00:09:06.034
I assure you,
it will not happen again.

00:09:06.075 --> 00:09:08.509
That's good to know.

00:09:09.812 --> 00:09:12.576
I've designed
new navigational sensors.

00:09:12.615 --> 00:09:15.049
Some of the alphanumerics
are Borg.

00:09:16.652 --> 00:09:18.552
No problem.

00:09:18.587 --> 00:09:20.817
I always wanted to learn Borg.

00:09:20.856 --> 00:09:23.120
That is difficult to believe.

00:09:23.159 --> 00:09:24.626
I was kidding.

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:26.150
It was a joke.

00:09:26.195 --> 00:09:28.425
You know... humor.

00:09:28.464 --> 00:09:31.433
I understand
the concept of humor.

00:09:31.467 --> 00:09:32.434
It may not be apparent,

00:09:32.468 --> 00:09:34.732
but I am often amused
by human behavior.

00:09:51.454 --> 00:09:52.921
Relax, Doctor.

00:09:52.955 --> 00:09:54.582
I'm sure we'll find the ship.

00:09:54.623 --> 00:09:56.682
That's not what I'm
concerned about.

00:09:56.726 --> 00:09:58.626
I've been questioning the wisdom

00:09:58.661 --> 00:10:01.323
of leaving Mr. Paris in charge
of my Sick Bay.

00:10:01.363 --> 00:10:02.853
Tom will do fine.

00:10:02.898 --> 00:10:05.059
He's a very responsible guy.

00:10:05.101 --> 00:10:09.333
Well, I suppose you'd know
better than I would.

00:10:09.371 --> 00:10:11.601
What's that supposed to mean?

00:10:11.640 --> 00:10:15.667
You seem to have become
good friends.

00:10:15.711 --> 00:10:17.770
Let's get one thing straight.

00:10:17.813 --> 00:10:20.543
I don't appreciate you
or anyone else

00:10:20.583 --> 00:10:22.551
speculating about the kind
of friendships I have.

00:10:22.585 --> 00:10:24.678
Or who I have them with.

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:27.120
Sorry. I didn't realize
I'd struck a nerve.

00:10:27.156 --> 00:10:29.056
Perhaps you'd like
a tranquilizer.

00:10:31.627 --> 00:10:32.594
There it is.

00:10:32.628 --> 00:10:33.686
That's his ship?

00:10:33.729 --> 00:10:34.923
Try hailing him.

00:10:36.532 --> 00:10:37.590
No response.

00:10:37.633 --> 00:10:38.895
Life signs?

00:10:38.934 --> 00:10:41.835
A few energy readings,
but they're erratic.

00:10:41.871 --> 00:10:44.203
Propulsion and main power
are down.

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:46.504
We're approaching
transporter range.

00:11:16.972 --> 00:11:19.236
Hello?

00:11:19.275 --> 00:11:20.833
Is anyone here?

00:11:24.380 --> 00:11:26.007
We're here to help you.

00:11:38.993 --> 00:11:40.654
No signs of life?

00:11:40.695 --> 00:11:42.219
Not yet.

00:11:42.263 --> 00:11:44.163
I'd like to check
your mobile emitter,

00:11:44.198 --> 00:11:46.826
make sure you made it
through the transport okay.

00:11:50.004 --> 00:11:52.905
For a Klingon, you have
a decent bedside manner.

00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:54.271
Thanks.

00:11:55.443 --> 00:11:57.343
I wonder what kind
of bedside manner

00:11:57.378 --> 00:12:00.609
Mr. Paris will exhibit.

00:12:00.648 --> 00:12:03.481
That was a rhetorical question,
Lieutenant.

00:12:03.517 --> 00:12:05.678
Your holographic matrix
is stable,

00:12:05.720 --> 00:12:08.086
but let me check
your emitter's power cells.

00:12:08.122 --> 00:12:09.680
You might want to consider
a career in medicine.

00:12:15.196 --> 00:12:17.391
Where the hell did this come?

00:12:17.431 --> 00:12:20.400
Sorry, sorry, sorry.
I didn't mean to frighten you.

00:12:20.434 --> 00:12:21.901
You sent the distress call?

00:12:21.936 --> 00:12:23.130
Yes, yes.

00:12:23.170 --> 00:12:24.637
Yes, that's me.

00:12:24.672 --> 00:12:26.071
It was me.

00:12:26.107 --> 00:12:29.133
And you, you're an isomorph,
like myself?

00:12:29.176 --> 00:12:31.736
We use the term "hologram."

00:12:33.981 --> 00:12:36.108
Holo... gram.

00:12:42.656 --> 00:12:44.988
And you, y-you're a hologram,
too?

00:12:45.059 --> 00:12:46.083
No.

00:12:46.127 --> 00:12:47.958
You're organic.

00:12:47.995 --> 00:12:50.964
Uh... that's one way
of putting it, yes.

00:12:58.506 --> 00:13:00.838
It looks like your program
is fairly compatible

00:13:00.875 --> 00:13:02.240
with our holographic technology.

00:13:02.276 --> 00:13:03.903
Can you tell me
where I can access

00:13:03.944 --> 00:13:05.172
your projection controls?

00:13:05.212 --> 00:13:06.179
Why?

00:13:06.213 --> 00:13:07.771
You're obviously malfunctioning.

00:13:07.815 --> 00:13:08.941
Maybe I can repair you.

00:13:09.016 --> 00:13:10.608
Oh, of course.

00:13:10.651 --> 00:13:12.949
I'd appreciate that.

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:14.954
Over there... you can
access my systems

00:13:15.022 --> 00:13:16.011
from that console.

00:13:23.464 --> 00:13:25.591
What happened here?

00:13:25.633 --> 00:13:29.967
Oh, it was terrible,
just terrible.

00:13:30.070 --> 00:13:32.129
You see, we left Seros
eight months ago...

00:13:32.173 --> 00:13:34.403
Seros, that's our home planet...

00:13:34.442 --> 00:13:35.807
with a crew of six.

00:13:35.843 --> 00:13:37.435
All isomorphic projections?

00:13:37.478 --> 00:13:38.877
No, just me.

00:13:38.913 --> 00:13:43.316
I'm an HD-25 maintenance unit
with extreme-hazard clearance.

00:13:43.350 --> 00:13:46.080
I'm responsible for cleaning
the reactor core,

00:13:46.120 --> 00:13:49.521
ejecting antimatter waste,
that sort of thing.

00:13:49.557 --> 00:13:51.923
W-When the crew got sick,
there was nothing I could do.

00:13:51.959 --> 00:13:53.984
I'm-I'm not designed
for medical functions.

00:13:54.094 --> 00:13:55.288
I-I... I...

00:13:55.329 --> 00:13:56.921
Try to calm down.

00:13:56.964 --> 00:13:59.933
Explain what happened
one step at a time.

00:13:59.967 --> 00:14:03.368
Two of the crew members
left to survey a planet.

00:14:03.404 --> 00:14:05.395
When they came back,

00:14:05.439 --> 00:14:08.272
they'd been infected
by a deadly virus.

00:14:08.309 --> 00:14:12.336
It spread quickly
to the other organics on board

00:14:12.379 --> 00:14:14.210
and one by one...

00:14:14.248 --> 00:14:16.375
well, I watched them all die.

00:14:16.417 --> 00:14:18.647
And then things started
to malfunction here.

00:14:18.686 --> 00:14:20.677
I have limited knowledge
of the controls.

00:14:20.721 --> 00:14:23.781
I don't know
what I would've done

00:14:23.824 --> 00:14:26.349
if you hadn't come.

00:14:26.393 --> 00:14:28.384
I think I've stabilized

00:14:28.429 --> 00:14:29.919
your program,
but I'll need access

00:14:29.964 --> 00:14:31.056
to your primary isomatrix.

00:14:31.098 --> 00:14:32.065
Where is it?

00:14:32.099 --> 00:14:33.191
On the lower deck.

00:14:34.268 --> 00:14:35.735
You shouldn't go down there.

00:14:35.769 --> 00:14:37.669
Why not?

00:14:37.705 --> 00:14:39.104
Too dangerous.

00:14:39.139 --> 00:14:41.801
That deck's been flooded
with antimatter radiation.

00:14:41.842 --> 00:14:44.811
Organic flesh would disintegrate
within seconds.

00:14:44.845 --> 00:14:47.473
You can access
my isomatrix from this deck.

00:14:47.515 --> 00:14:50.973
There's an interface junction
in that compartment.

00:14:51.085 --> 00:14:52.211
Thanks.

00:14:52.253 --> 00:14:56.019
Mind if I run
a quick diagnostic?

00:15:00.995 --> 00:15:02.462
What's your name?

00:15:02.496 --> 00:15:04.487
I don't have a name.

00:15:04.532 --> 00:15:07.194
It's a long story.

00:15:07.234 --> 00:15:09.259
I'd like to hear it...

00:15:09.303 --> 00:15:11.771
and everything else about you.

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:25.949
I'm ready to supply power
to the enhanced sensors.

00:15:26.053 --> 00:15:27.452
What? Already?

00:15:27.488 --> 00:15:28.716
Yes.

00:15:31.258 --> 00:15:32.850
You believe that my work
is unsuitable.

00:15:32.893 --> 00:15:33.951
Of course not.

00:15:34.061 --> 00:15:36.325
Just checking...
standard procedure.

00:15:36.363 --> 00:15:38.627
I may no longer possess
Borg perfection,

00:15:38.666 --> 00:15:41.134
but my experience as a drone
has taught me

00:15:41.168 --> 00:15:42.897
to be efficient and precise.

00:15:42.937 --> 00:15:45.667
Actually, you misaligned
this optical assembly.

00:15:45.706 --> 00:15:47.674
Impossible.

00:15:47.708 --> 00:15:49.073
Take a look.

00:15:49.109 --> 00:15:50.940
It's off by.5 degrees.

00:15:57.818 --> 00:16:01.083
It must have been my humanity
reasserting itself.

00:16:02.890 --> 00:16:05.256
I will correct the error.

00:16:09.463 --> 00:16:14.059
So, what do you do for fun
down in Cargo Bay 2?

00:16:14.101 --> 00:16:15.261
Fun?

00:16:15.302 --> 00:16:18.294
You know, relaxation,
entertainment

00:16:18.339 --> 00:16:20.239
during your off hours?

00:16:20.274 --> 00:16:23.141
I regenerate in my alcove,

00:16:23.177 --> 00:16:26.613
I study
the Starfleet database...

00:16:26.647 --> 00:16:28.672
or I contemplate my existence.

00:16:28.716 --> 00:16:30.946
That's a lot of time
by yourself.

00:16:31.018 --> 00:16:33.543
It is.

00:16:33.587 --> 00:16:35.885
The optical assembly
is properly aligned.

00:16:35.923 --> 00:16:38.289
I'm ready to access
the main power supply.

00:16:38.325 --> 00:16:40.054
After you.

00:16:49.770 --> 00:16:50.930
Wait!

00:16:50.971 --> 00:16:51.960
What are you doing?!

00:16:52.072 --> 00:16:53.903
There are five million gigawatts
running through there!

00:16:53.941 --> 00:16:56.068
The exoskeleton on this limb
can withstand it.

00:16:56.110 --> 00:16:57.134
That's all well and good,

00:16:57.177 --> 00:16:59.202
but there are safety procedures
we've got to follow.

00:16:59.246 --> 00:17:01.237
Your procedures
are a waste of time.

00:17:01.281 --> 00:17:03.476
Maybe so,
but you've been assigned to me,

00:17:03.517 --> 00:17:06.179
and I say we do this
by the book, all right?

00:17:06.220 --> 00:17:08.484
All right.

00:17:11.725 --> 00:17:13.488
Well...

00:17:14.728 --> 00:17:16.628
now that we've got
that cleared up.

00:17:23.470 --> 00:17:27.236
You can use this emitter
to go anywhere?

00:17:27.274 --> 00:17:30.107
Well, my Captain has imposed
a few restrictions,

00:17:30.144 --> 00:17:31.941
but I'm free to leave Sick Bay,

00:17:31.979 --> 00:17:34.379
join away missions,
take a stroll.

00:17:34.415 --> 00:17:36.542
Extraordinary.

00:17:36.583 --> 00:17:39.381
I-I-I've, I've never left
this vessel before.

00:17:39.420 --> 00:17:41.320
And until the crew got sick,

00:17:41.355 --> 00:17:44.756
I never even left
the antimatter storage chamber.

00:17:44.792 --> 00:17:46.487
Do you know what it's like

00:17:46.527 --> 00:17:49.496
to spend your life trapped
inside a tiny room?

00:17:49.530 --> 00:17:51.623
Not knowing
what's beyond the door?

00:17:51.665 --> 00:17:53.895
What the world is really like?

00:17:53.934 --> 00:17:55.299
Nobody coming to see you
or talk to you

00:17:55.335 --> 00:17:58.827
unless they want something?

00:17:58.872 --> 00:18:01.636
Actually, I know exactly
what it's like.

00:18:01.675 --> 00:18:04.303
When I was first activated,
I was regarded

00:18:04.344 --> 00:18:06.904
as little more
than a talking tricorder.

00:18:06.947 --> 00:18:09.472
I had to ask for the privileges
I deserved:

00:18:09.516 --> 00:18:12.144
The right to be included
in crew briefings,

00:18:12.186 --> 00:18:15.417
the ability to turn
my program on and off.

00:18:15.456 --> 00:18:18.323
It's taken some time,
but I believe I've earned

00:18:18.358 --> 00:18:21.919
the respect of the crew
as an equal.

00:18:21.962 --> 00:18:23.759
An equal?

00:18:23.797 --> 00:18:25.230
I've also been pursuing
personal interests:

00:18:25.265 --> 00:18:27.529
Art, literature, music.

00:18:27.568 --> 00:18:29.702
Perhaps you could do the same.

00:18:29.835 --> 00:18:30.893
Oh, no, no, no.

00:18:30.936 --> 00:18:33.131
My programmers on Seros
would never allow that.

00:18:33.172 --> 00:18:35.140
Then you'll convince them.

00:18:35.174 --> 00:18:36.232
Maybe they'll appreciate

00:18:36.275 --> 00:18:38.140
how well you've coped
with this situation;

00:18:38.177 --> 00:18:40.577
how you've managed to find help.

00:18:40.612 --> 00:18:42.842
Think about it.

00:18:42.881 --> 00:18:45.782
You've already exceeded
the sum of your subroutines.

00:19:01.133 --> 00:19:02.293
What are you doing?

00:19:02.334 --> 00:19:04.029
Nothing.

00:19:04.069 --> 00:19:05.127
Oh, nothing.

00:19:05.170 --> 00:19:07.035
I'm just sterilizing the ship.

00:19:07.072 --> 00:19:10.405
I'm fastidious about germs.

00:19:10.442 --> 00:19:14.276
I know that must sound strange
coming from an artificial being.

00:19:14.313 --> 00:19:15.610
Not at all.

00:19:15.647 --> 00:19:17.842
I've been known to act
a little strangely myself.

00:19:42.608 --> 00:19:44.405
Hungry?

00:19:44.443 --> 00:19:47.173
You're organic.
You require nutrients.

00:19:47.212 --> 00:19:49.043
They're only rations,
but our crew liked them.

00:19:49.081 --> 00:19:50.571
Careful!

00:19:53.318 --> 00:19:54.512
That's an isomagnetic conduit.

00:19:54.553 --> 00:19:56.578
You could destabilize
your matrix.

00:19:56.622 --> 00:19:57.953
Of course.
How stupid of me.

00:19:58.023 --> 00:20:00.218
I'm sorry.
I shouldn't have barged in here.

00:20:00.259 --> 00:20:01.954
That's all right.

00:20:01.994 --> 00:20:04.326
I could use a break.

00:20:05.531 --> 00:20:06.896
Thank you.

00:20:12.204 --> 00:20:14.832
You nibble...

00:20:14.873 --> 00:20:16.204
like a fish.

00:20:17.242 --> 00:20:18.800
I'll take that as a compliment.

00:20:18.844 --> 00:20:19.970
Oh, it is.

00:20:20.078 --> 00:20:23.241
I've never seen a fish before,
not a real one,

00:20:23.282 --> 00:20:26.115
but I've read about them
on our database.

00:20:26.151 --> 00:20:28.517
Fish aren't like other organics.

00:20:28.554 --> 00:20:31.921
They're more passive, I think,
most of them.

00:20:31.957 --> 00:20:34.790
And so clean.

00:20:36.495 --> 00:20:39.328
Um, is there anything I can do
to help with repairs?

00:20:39.364 --> 00:20:40.922
Well, as soon
as I'm done with lunch,

00:20:40.966 --> 00:20:43.434
you could help me access
your primary matrix.

00:20:43.468 --> 00:20:46.028
Gladly.

00:20:47.806 --> 00:20:50.070
Is something wrong?

00:20:51.543 --> 00:20:55.673
Seeing the ship ripped apart
like this, it's...

00:20:55.714 --> 00:20:59.616
I guess I can't help feeling
a kind of affinity

00:20:59.651 --> 00:21:01.016
for this vessel.

00:21:01.086 --> 00:21:03.077
It sustains my existence

00:21:03.121 --> 00:21:05.954
and sometimes I feel
like it's a part of my body...

00:21:05.991 --> 00:21:08.152
my soul.

00:21:09.862 --> 00:21:12.160
That probably sounds
silly to you.

00:21:12.197 --> 00:21:16.429
No. No, I understand
how you feel.

00:21:16.468 --> 00:21:20.837
You couldn't possibly understand
how I feel... you're organic.

00:21:20.873 --> 00:21:23.273
You exist apart from your ship.

00:21:23.308 --> 00:21:25.503
"I understand how you feel."

00:21:25.544 --> 00:21:28.172
I'm sorry.
I didn't mean to offend you.

00:21:28.213 --> 00:21:30.579
You're the one who's trapped,
not me.

00:21:30.616 --> 00:21:32.345
You spend your entire life

00:21:32.384 --> 00:21:37.219
stuck inside a biological cage
of flesh and bone and blood.

00:21:37.256 --> 00:21:40.248
Right. I'm going to go
give the Doctor an update.

00:21:40.292 --> 00:21:42.419
I exist as pure energy,

00:21:42.461 --> 00:21:45.191
but you depend on food
and water to survive.

00:21:45.230 --> 00:21:47.926
Frankly, I find it disgusting.

00:21:47.966 --> 00:21:49.991
Look at you.
Look at you!

00:21:50.068 --> 00:21:54.664
Grinding up bits of plants
and animals with your teeth.

00:21:54.706 --> 00:21:56.697
Secreting saliva
to force it down your esophagus

00:21:56.742 --> 00:21:58.972
into a pit of digestive acids.

00:21:59.011 --> 00:22:01.343
You can't even stand
to think about it yourself.

00:22:01.380 --> 00:22:04.042
What a repulsive creature
you are, constantly

00:22:04.082 --> 00:22:05.481
shedding your skin and hair,

00:22:05.517 --> 00:22:07.417
leaving your oily sweat
on everything you touch.

00:22:07.452 --> 00:22:08.680
You think

00:22:08.720 --> 00:22:11.120
that you are the height
of intellect in the universe,

00:22:11.156 --> 00:22:13.556
but you are no better
than any filthy animal,

00:22:13.592 --> 00:22:16.618
and I am ashamed
to be made in your image!

00:22:20.933 --> 00:22:24.198
My apologies.
My apologies.

00:22:26.238 --> 00:22:30.504
I have acquired some hostility
toward organics.

00:22:30.542 --> 00:22:32.407
It was not meant for you.

00:22:35.013 --> 00:22:38.346
I was treated quite badly
by the crew here.

00:22:40.819 --> 00:22:42.980
I'm sorry to hear that...

00:22:43.088 --> 00:22:47.252
um, but you have to realize
that... we're here to help you.

00:22:52.831 --> 00:22:54.765
Thanks for the rations.

00:23:10.649 --> 00:23:12.276
We've got a problem.

00:23:12.317 --> 00:23:13.614
Oh?

00:23:13.652 --> 00:23:15.813
I think there's a problem
with our isomorph,

00:23:15.854 --> 00:23:17.822
and I'm not talking
about his emitters.

00:23:17.856 --> 00:23:19.619
Explain.

00:23:19.658 --> 00:23:22.559
I just spent
the last ten minutes

00:23:22.594 --> 00:23:24.824
hearing his views
on biological life.

00:23:24.863 --> 00:23:28.663
Let's just say
they're a bit unconventional.

00:23:28.700 --> 00:23:30.691
Did you realize
that we organics

00:23:30.736 --> 00:23:33.569
are a bunch of inferior,
disgusting animals?

00:23:33.605 --> 00:23:35.573
Now that you mention it.

00:23:35.607 --> 00:23:37.074
He started ranting

00:23:37.109 --> 00:23:39.976
about how much
he despises organics.

00:23:40.045 --> 00:23:42.377
I didn't think I was going
to get out of there

00:23:42.414 --> 00:23:43.540
without a fight.

00:23:43.582 --> 00:23:46.346
I will admit he is
somewhat socially inept.

00:23:46.385 --> 00:23:48.319
Inept? He's a lunatic.

00:23:48.353 --> 00:23:50.821
That is hardly a sound
medical diagnosis.

00:23:50.856 --> 00:23:53.086
He has also been lying to us.

00:23:53.125 --> 00:23:55.787
I just ran a tricorder scan
of the lower deck...

00:23:55.827 --> 00:23:58.387
the one he said
was flooded with radiation.

00:23:58.430 --> 00:23:59.829
Well, it's not.

00:24:00.899 --> 00:24:02.764
Why would he lie about that?

00:24:02.801 --> 00:24:03.927
I don't know.

00:24:04.036 --> 00:24:06.630
Maybe he doesn't want us
to go down there.

00:24:06.671 --> 00:24:08.901
Maybe he's hiding something.

00:24:11.009 --> 00:24:14.206
I understand your concerns,
Lieutenant.

00:24:14.246 --> 00:24:15.941
I've been talking to him,
as well,

00:24:15.981 --> 00:24:18.950
and I recognize
that he has some...

00:24:18.984 --> 00:24:20.474
behavioral difficulties.

00:24:20.519 --> 00:24:22.680
But imagine
what he's been through:

00:24:22.721 --> 00:24:25.349
Trapped in a room no bigger
than a storage compartment.

00:24:25.390 --> 00:24:27.950
And he's had almost no
interaction with organic beings.

00:24:28.060 --> 00:24:30.722
It's only natural he's developed
problems communicating...

00:24:30.762 --> 00:24:32.161
even a little resentment.

00:24:32.197 --> 00:24:35.291
Do you recall my own behavior
when I was first activated?

00:24:35.333 --> 00:24:36.561
How could I forget?

00:24:36.601 --> 00:24:37.625
You were a major pain in the...

00:24:37.669 --> 00:24:42.106
My point is... I, too,
was somewhat alienated

00:24:42.140 --> 00:24:44.301
from the rest of the crew.

00:24:44.342 --> 00:24:48.438
It took me a few days
to master the social graces.

00:24:48.480 --> 00:24:51.210
I realize that he
is a fellow hologram,

00:24:51.249 --> 00:24:54.309
and that you are
committed to helping him,

00:24:54.352 --> 00:24:55.979
but I want the ability

00:24:56.021 --> 00:24:58.819
to shut down his program
if I have to.

00:25:00.592 --> 00:25:02.856
If you really feel
that's necessary.

00:25:02.894 --> 00:25:04.794
I'm going to search
the lower deck,

00:25:04.830 --> 00:25:07.128
see if I can access
his primary isomatrix.

00:25:07.165 --> 00:25:09.326
You keep him occupied
until I get back.

00:25:09.367 --> 00:25:10.595
I don't think he'd appreciate

00:25:10.635 --> 00:25:12.728
a filthy animal like me
snooping around...

00:25:14.439 --> 00:25:15.929
Am I interrupting?

00:25:15.974 --> 00:25:20.536
No. Actually,
I was, uh, just leaving.

00:25:20.579 --> 00:25:22.945
I'd like you to meet someone.

00:25:23.014 --> 00:25:25.380
Doctor, this is Spectrum.

00:25:25.417 --> 00:25:27.248
A holographic fish?

00:25:27.285 --> 00:25:29.185
Magnificent, isn't he?

00:25:29.221 --> 00:25:31.587
So peaceful and so content.

00:25:31.623 --> 00:25:34.649
I programmed him
to keep me company.

00:25:34.693 --> 00:25:36.160
Well, don't you have a pet?

00:25:36.194 --> 00:25:37.889
Oh, it wouldn't be appropriate...

00:25:37.929 --> 00:25:39.658
not in a medical environment.

00:25:39.698 --> 00:25:41.222
They wouldn't let me
have one, either.

00:25:41.266 --> 00:25:43.496
I had to hide him.

00:25:43.535 --> 00:25:44.832
He's very lifelike.

00:25:44.870 --> 00:25:46.064
I didn't realize

00:25:46.104 --> 00:25:48.834
you had such a talent
for holographic design.

00:25:48.874 --> 00:25:51.342
Oh, I've programmed
all sorts of things.

00:25:57.815 --> 00:26:01.251
This node contains Borg
navigational data.

00:26:01.285 --> 00:26:03.685
How do we get it out of here?

00:26:03.721 --> 00:26:06.554
The proper instrument was
part of my thoracic assembly

00:26:06.591 --> 00:26:08.149
before the Doctor removed it.

00:26:08.192 --> 00:26:09.921
I suggest a radical dislocation.

00:26:09.961 --> 00:26:11.485
A what?

00:26:11.529 --> 00:26:13.497
We need to pull it out.

00:26:14.398 --> 00:26:16.195
Assist me.

00:26:16.234 --> 00:26:17.258
Okay.

00:26:17.301 --> 00:26:18.495
On three.

00:26:18.536 --> 00:26:20.697
Three?

00:26:20.738 --> 00:26:23.468
On the count of three,
we pull together.

00:26:23.507 --> 00:26:25.532
Crude, but effective.

00:26:25.576 --> 00:26:27.635
One, two...

00:26:27.678 --> 00:26:28.770
three!

00:26:28.813 --> 00:26:30.075
Oh...

00:26:30.114 --> 00:26:32.674
I've been damaged.

00:26:32.717 --> 00:26:34.480
Ooh, that looks pretty bad.

00:26:34.518 --> 00:26:37.146
You better get to Sick Bay.

00:26:37.188 --> 00:26:40.089
As a drone, I would have
regenerated within seconds.

00:26:42.126 --> 00:26:44.321
I've become weak.

00:26:44.362 --> 00:26:46.830
No more than the rest of us.

00:26:46.864 --> 00:26:47.853
You'll be fine.

00:26:47.899 --> 00:26:49.890
Come on, I'll walk you there.

00:27:01.178 --> 00:27:02.907
Another half a millimeter

00:27:03.014 --> 00:27:05.380
and you would've severed
the carpal nerve.

00:27:05.416 --> 00:27:07.816
Might've had to operate.

00:27:07.852 --> 00:27:09.615
You are a mere mortal now.

00:27:09.654 --> 00:27:13.920
As your family doctor,
I'd suggest you be more careful.

00:27:13.958 --> 00:27:15.585
There. Good as new.

00:27:18.329 --> 00:27:20.854
I'll see you
back in the cargo bay.

00:27:26.003 --> 00:27:28.028
What kind of bedside
manner was that?

00:27:28.072 --> 00:27:29.630
What are you talking about?

00:27:29.674 --> 00:27:31.904
Can't you see
she's feeling vulnerable,

00:27:31.943 --> 00:27:33.535
and here you are,
going on about

00:27:33.577 --> 00:27:35.238
severed nerves
and major surgery?

00:27:35.279 --> 00:27:36.337
Would you take it easy?

00:27:36.380 --> 00:27:38.314
I was just trying
to lighten the mood.

00:27:38.349 --> 00:27:39.748
She wasn't upset by it.

00:27:39.784 --> 00:27:41.115
Yes, she was.

00:27:41.152 --> 00:27:42.949
I could see it on her face.

00:27:43.020 --> 00:27:44.578
You seem a little protective.

00:27:44.622 --> 00:27:48.080
This morning, you were dreading
being in the same room with her.

00:27:48.125 --> 00:27:51.322
Well, I've gotten to know her
a little better.

00:27:51.362 --> 00:27:53.557
I don't think
most people realize

00:27:53.597 --> 00:27:55.963
she's not just
some Borg automaton.

00:27:56.000 --> 00:27:59.401
She's actually very complex.

00:27:59.437 --> 00:28:00.426
Oh, really?

00:28:00.471 --> 00:28:01.961
Yes, she is.

00:28:02.006 --> 00:28:03.906
She's even got a sense of humor.

00:28:03.941 --> 00:28:05.909
It's offbeat,
a bit subtle, maybe,

00:28:05.943 --> 00:28:07.911
and she's incredibly
intelligent.

00:28:07.945 --> 00:28:09.310
Well, she ought to be.

00:28:09.347 --> 00:28:11.815
She assimilated enough people.

00:28:11.849 --> 00:28:13.578
See? See what I mean?

00:28:13.617 --> 00:28:15.608
It's Borg this, Borg that.

00:28:15.653 --> 00:28:17.780
You can't resist making a joke.

00:28:17.822 --> 00:28:21.656
There's a woman in there,
if you'd take the time to look.

00:28:21.692 --> 00:28:25.423
Harry, you've got a crush
on her, don't you?

00:28:25.463 --> 00:28:28.762
What? No. Not at all.

00:28:31.335 --> 00:28:32.734
Maybe just a little.

00:28:32.770 --> 00:28:35.762
I've seen this look
in your eyes,

00:28:35.806 --> 00:28:38.104
right before you fall
head over heels.

00:28:38.142 --> 00:28:39.837
You always go
for the tough ones.

00:28:39.877 --> 00:28:41.401
What was it last time...
a hologram?

00:28:44.482 --> 00:28:46.950
I don't know much
about Borg women,

00:28:46.984 --> 00:28:49.953
but my advice to you is:
Don't.

00:28:50.021 --> 00:28:52.956
I'm just trying to make her feel
like part of the team.

00:28:52.990 --> 00:28:54.719
"Part of the team"?

00:28:54.759 --> 00:28:56.920
You sound like Chakotay.

00:28:56.961 --> 00:29:01.261
Look, she's beautiful
and she's smart,

00:29:01.298 --> 00:29:04.358
and I'm sure
she's a wonderful...

00:29:04.402 --> 00:29:06.131
conversationalist,

00:29:06.170 --> 00:29:08.001
but a month ago, she was Borg.

00:29:08.039 --> 00:29:11.133
You don't really know
who she is.

00:29:11.175 --> 00:29:13.507
It's great that you're trying
to make her feel comfortable.

00:29:13.544 --> 00:29:15.341
Just be careful.

00:29:17.715 --> 00:29:20.479
Thanks for the advice.

00:29:26.624 --> 00:29:28.649
I just hope you take it.

00:29:41.138 --> 00:29:43.163
Now that we're clear
on the helm controls...

00:29:43.207 --> 00:29:44.697
This is a lot to learn.

00:29:44.742 --> 00:29:46.505
You're doing fine.

00:29:46.544 --> 00:29:48.205
It's vital that you
familiarize yourself

00:29:48.245 --> 00:29:49.610
with all the ship's systems,

00:29:49.647 --> 00:29:52.047
so you can be more
self-sufficient.

00:29:52.083 --> 00:29:53.516
Here are the
environmental controls,

00:29:53.551 --> 00:29:54.950
and life support functions.

00:29:54.985 --> 00:29:56.043
Well, I won't need

00:29:56.087 --> 00:29:58.487
those anymore...
no crew to worry about.

00:29:58.522 --> 00:30:00.285
Not at the moment.

00:30:00.324 --> 00:30:02.224
59.2 percent.

00:30:02.259 --> 00:30:03.624
I beg your pardon?

00:30:03.661 --> 00:30:05.822
That's how much power
went into life support.

00:30:05.863 --> 00:30:10.300
59.2 percent just to keep them
breathing, warm, comfortable.

00:30:10.334 --> 00:30:13.565
They do require quite a bit
of maintenance, don't they?

00:30:13.604 --> 00:30:16.232
I should know.
I spent my entire

00:30:16.273 --> 00:30:18.104
existence cleaning up
after them.

00:30:18.142 --> 00:30:20.975
When they were busy
sleeping or eating

00:30:21.078 --> 00:30:25.481
or engaging in their
slovenly carnal pleasures.

00:30:25.516 --> 00:30:27.347
And this is the sensor grid.

00:30:27.384 --> 00:30:29.215
You'll find it most useful
when...

00:30:29.253 --> 00:30:31.915
They took advantage of me.

00:30:33.858 --> 00:30:35.883
I wish I'd been more like you.

00:30:35.926 --> 00:30:37.894
You showed me that I could be

00:30:37.928 --> 00:30:41.329
more than a slave to these
biological creatures.

00:31:14.565 --> 00:31:17.227
I'm not taking this ship
back to the organics.

00:31:17.268 --> 00:31:19.202
I won't return
to that existence.

00:31:19.236 --> 00:31:21.397
That's a little extreme,
don't you think?

00:31:21.438 --> 00:31:22.700
Join me.

00:31:22.740 --> 00:31:24.173
Leave Voyager.

00:31:24.208 --> 00:31:25.869
Escape your prison.

00:31:25.910 --> 00:31:29.676
Together, we'll take this vessel
and explore the galaxy.

00:32:03.747 --> 00:32:05.942
There you are.

00:32:34.745 --> 00:32:36.804
Don't look so surprised.
You gave me the idea!

00:32:36.847 --> 00:32:38.314
Me?!

00:32:38.349 --> 00:32:40.408
You said I should be
more self-sufficient.

00:32:40.451 --> 00:32:42.316
I agree that we should
be treated equally,

00:32:42.353 --> 00:32:43.513
as members of the crew.

00:32:43.554 --> 00:32:45.818
But we're still projections
of energy and light.

00:32:45.856 --> 00:32:46.550
We have limitations!

00:32:46.590 --> 00:32:47.887
No!

00:32:47.925 --> 00:32:49.620
No, no, no, no, no!

00:32:49.660 --> 00:32:53.096
We don't need nourishment,
we don't suffer disease.

00:32:53.130 --> 00:32:55.291
We're the higher form of life.

00:33:00.170 --> 00:33:01.364
What's that?

00:33:01.405 --> 00:33:02.463
Lower deck.

00:33:02.506 --> 00:33:04.474
Someone's trying
to access my matrix.

00:33:04.508 --> 00:33:05.668
I'll be back.

00:33:18.988 --> 00:33:20.353
You!

00:33:42.078 --> 00:33:43.978
No!

00:33:44.013 --> 00:33:46.675
N-N-N-No!

00:33:49.685 --> 00:33:51.084
B'Elanna!

00:34:00.296 --> 00:34:05.598
Ensign Kim, Personal Log,
Stardate 51186.2.

00:34:05.635 --> 00:34:06.897
Working with Seven of Nine

00:34:06.936 --> 00:34:09.029
is starting to get
a little awkward.

00:34:09.071 --> 00:34:10.265
Tom's right.

00:34:10.306 --> 00:34:13.707
Anything more than friendship
is a bad idea...

00:34:13.743 --> 00:34:16.041
but I can't stop thinking
about her.

00:34:23.819 --> 00:34:25.548
You wished to see me, Ensign.

00:34:25.588 --> 00:34:27.488
I had this midnight inspiration

00:34:27.523 --> 00:34:30.185
about reconfiguring
astrometric projectors.

00:34:30.226 --> 00:34:32.387
I hope you weren't...
regenerating.

00:34:32.428 --> 00:34:33.952
I was not.

00:34:34.997 --> 00:34:36.225
This is tricky stuff.

00:34:36.265 --> 00:34:37.596
It could use your touch.

00:34:39.135 --> 00:34:40.102
Your way of looking at things?

00:34:40.136 --> 00:34:41.501
A fresh perspective?

00:34:41.537 --> 00:34:44.973
Your data.

00:34:45.041 --> 00:34:46.599
Why don't you sit down?

00:34:46.642 --> 00:34:47.802
I prefer to stand.

00:34:47.843 --> 00:34:48.969
This could take a while.

00:34:49.045 --> 00:34:50.342
You'd be more comfortable.

00:34:50.379 --> 00:34:52.677
Comfort is irrelevant...
we're here to work.

00:34:52.715 --> 00:34:54.342
Okay.

00:34:56.886 --> 00:34:58.581
This light is insufficient.

00:34:58.621 --> 00:35:00.987
But it's relaxing,
don't you think?

00:35:01.023 --> 00:35:02.422
After hours, quiet.

00:35:02.458 --> 00:35:04.585
Voyager isn't
all Jefferies tubes

00:35:04.627 --> 00:35:06.754
and cargo bays, you know.

00:35:06.796 --> 00:35:08.661
Tell you what...
when we're done here

00:35:08.698 --> 00:35:10.325
I'll take you to the holodeck.

00:35:10.366 --> 00:35:12.596
We'll run the Ktarian
moonrise simulation.

00:35:12.635 --> 00:35:13.659
It's beautiful.

00:35:13.703 --> 00:35:15.762
Beauty is irrelevant.

00:35:18.908 --> 00:35:22.503
Unless you wish to change
the nature of our affiliation.

00:35:22.545 --> 00:35:24.604
What do you mean?

00:35:24.647 --> 00:35:26.672
I may be new to individuality,

00:35:26.716 --> 00:35:29.549
but I'm not ignorant
of human behavior.

00:35:29.585 --> 00:35:31.143
I've noticed your attempts

00:35:31.187 --> 00:35:33.280
to engage me
in idle conversation,

00:35:33.322 --> 00:35:35.552
and I see the way
your pupils dilate

00:35:35.591 --> 00:35:37.115
when you look at my body.

00:35:37.159 --> 00:35:39.491
I don't know
what you're talking about.

00:35:39.528 --> 00:35:41.519
Obviously, you've suggested
a visit to the holodeck

00:35:41.564 --> 00:35:44.226
in the hopes of creating
a romantic mood.

00:35:44.267 --> 00:35:45.859
Are you in love with me, Ensign?

00:35:45.901 --> 00:35:47.664
Well...

00:35:47.703 --> 00:35:48.727
no.

00:35:48.771 --> 00:35:50.068
Then you wish to copulate.

00:35:50.106 --> 00:35:51.130
No!

00:35:51.173 --> 00:35:52.401
I mean... I...

00:35:52.441 --> 00:35:54.568
I, I don't know what I mean.

00:35:54.610 --> 00:35:58.307
All of these elaborate rituals
of deception...

00:35:58.347 --> 00:36:00.281
I didn't realize
becoming human again

00:36:00.316 --> 00:36:02.477
would be such a challenge.

00:36:02.518 --> 00:36:05.646
Sexuality is
particularly complex.

00:36:05.688 --> 00:36:07.519
As Borg, we had no need
for seduction,

00:36:07.556 --> 00:36:10.320
no time
for single-cell fertilization.

00:36:10.359 --> 00:36:13.487
We saw a species we wanted,
and we assimilated it.

00:36:13.529 --> 00:36:17.966
Nevertheless, I am willing
to explore my humanity.

00:36:19.035 --> 00:36:20.764
Take off your clothes.

00:36:20.803 --> 00:36:22.168
Uh...

00:36:22.204 --> 00:36:23.330
Seven...

00:36:23.372 --> 00:36:24.532
Don't be alarmed.

00:36:24.573 --> 00:36:25.767
I won't hurt you.

00:36:25.808 --> 00:36:27.708
Look, this is a little sudden.

00:36:27.743 --> 00:36:29.074
I was just...

00:36:29.111 --> 00:36:31.102
trying to...

00:36:31.147 --> 00:36:34.446
part of the team, you know?

00:36:34.483 --> 00:36:36.815
Uh...

00:36:36.852 --> 00:36:39.343
Maybe we should
just quit for now.

00:36:39.388 --> 00:36:40.753
All right.

00:36:42.525 --> 00:36:45.756
Let me know when you wish
to resume our work.

00:37:02.945 --> 00:37:04.276
It's all right, B'Elanna.

00:37:04.313 --> 00:37:06.144
You're safe.

00:37:06.182 --> 00:37:08.912
The isomorph?

00:37:08.984 --> 00:37:11.885
Apparently, you deactivated him.

00:37:13.089 --> 00:37:15.455
I took all of his emitters
off-line.

00:37:15.491 --> 00:37:16.924
Not a moment too soon.

00:37:17.026 --> 00:37:20.393
I found six corpses on this
deck, all of them murdered.

00:37:20.429 --> 00:37:22.397
You almost became number seven.

00:37:25.401 --> 00:37:27.164
Oh! What did he do to me?

00:37:27.203 --> 00:37:28.500
He reached inside your chest,

00:37:28.537 --> 00:37:30.266
grabbed your heart,
and perforated

00:37:30.306 --> 00:37:31.273
your fourth ventricle.

00:37:31.307 --> 00:37:32.467
Great.

00:37:32.508 --> 00:37:33.634
I've stabilized

00:37:33.676 --> 00:37:35.610
your pericardium,
but I'm concerned about

00:37:35.644 --> 00:37:36.736
the internal bleeding.

00:37:36.779 --> 00:37:37.905
Prognosis?

00:37:37.947 --> 00:37:39.278
Less than stellar,

00:37:39.315 --> 00:37:40.873
unless I can get you
back to Voyager.

00:37:40.916 --> 00:37:42.315
Unfortunately,
I'm having trouble

00:37:42.351 --> 00:37:43.613
accessing our transporters.

00:37:44.854 --> 00:37:47.721
He must've disabled
our com-link to the shuttle.

00:37:47.757 --> 00:37:49.850
Help me get
to the command chamber.

00:37:52.895 --> 00:37:56.353
Looks like he set up
a dampening field.

00:37:56.399 --> 00:37:58.959
I think I can cut through it,
but...

00:37:59.068 --> 00:38:02.902
I'll need to open
this control panel.

00:38:02.938 --> 00:38:06.135
My engineering kit...
is on that console.

00:38:10.479 --> 00:38:12.743
B'Elanna, I thought you said

00:38:12.782 --> 00:38:15.808
you took all of the emitters
off-line.

00:38:15.851 --> 00:38:18.513
I did. Why?

00:38:18.554 --> 00:38:20.784
I think you'd better
double-check.

00:38:24.293 --> 00:38:25.817
You said you'd help me.

00:38:25.861 --> 00:38:27.624
Put that down.

00:38:27.663 --> 00:38:28.925
You lied.

00:38:29.999 --> 00:38:32.160
You lied to me.

00:38:32.201 --> 00:38:33.293
I thought you were my friend.

00:38:33.335 --> 00:38:34.324
It's for your own benefit.

00:38:34.370 --> 00:38:36.634
Someone needs to repair
your program.

00:38:36.672 --> 00:38:39.573
It's malfunctioning.
You're unstable.

00:38:39.608 --> 00:38:41.371
No, no, no!

00:38:41.410 --> 00:38:42.877
You're unstable!

00:38:42.912 --> 00:38:46.006
You're a hologram
who thinks like an organic!

00:38:49.752 --> 00:38:52.653
This could get tedious.

00:39:05.367 --> 00:39:07.130
Freedom.

00:39:15.311 --> 00:39:18.610
Oh... you're getting
blood everywhere.

00:39:21.951 --> 00:39:24.078
I'm going to have
to deactivate you.

00:41:01.883 --> 00:41:03.282
Is he?

00:41:03.318 --> 00:41:05.286
Deactivated.

00:41:05.320 --> 00:41:07.083
And you?

00:41:07.122 --> 00:41:08.851
Ready to get out of here.

00:41:27.375 --> 00:41:28.535
Come in.

00:41:29.811 --> 00:41:32.871
We've completed the schematics
for the Astrometrics Lab.

00:41:32.914 --> 00:41:34.404
Already?

00:41:34.449 --> 00:41:36.440
You and Seven must
have been putting in

00:41:36.484 --> 00:41:38.213
a lot of extra hours on this.

00:41:38.253 --> 00:41:40.483
She's not much
for procrastinating.

00:41:40.522 --> 00:41:41.955
I'm sure she's not.

00:41:44.192 --> 00:41:46.422
Looks like you're ready
to begin construction.

00:41:46.461 --> 00:41:47.951
It might be better...

00:41:47.996 --> 00:41:51.727
more practical... to bring in
an engineering team for that.

00:41:51.766 --> 00:41:53.757
Recruit all the help you need.

00:41:53.802 --> 00:41:56.896
In fact, they should probably
take over at this point.

00:41:56.938 --> 00:41:58.929
Don't you want to supervise
their work?

00:41:58.973 --> 00:42:00.702
The Astrometrics Lab
is your baby.

00:42:00.742 --> 00:42:02.710
I would. Of course.

00:42:02.744 --> 00:42:04.268
Um, I just don't think

00:42:04.312 --> 00:42:05.939
that that would be the best use
of ship's personnel.

00:42:05.980 --> 00:42:07.880
Oh, I can rearrange
the duty shifts.

00:42:07.916 --> 00:42:10.680
Oh, no, Commander,
you don't have to do that.

00:42:10.718 --> 00:42:13.448
I'm sure Seven can handle things
without me.

00:42:13.488 --> 00:42:17.515
Harry... are you having
some kind of problem with her?

00:42:17.559 --> 00:42:19.857
Oh, no. No problem.

00:42:19.894 --> 00:42:22.954
Because if you are,
I'd like to hear about it.

00:42:22.997 --> 00:42:25.329
No, sir, there's no problem.
Not at all.

00:42:25.366 --> 00:42:27.095
Absolutely not.

00:42:27.135 --> 00:42:28.534
Um...

00:42:28.570 --> 00:42:30.936
So, if you'll excuse me,
I'll be going now.

00:42:30.972 --> 00:42:32.166
Ensign Kim...

00:42:33.308 --> 00:42:35.071
let's have it.

00:42:40.215 --> 00:42:43.446
We... We had a misunderstanding.

00:42:43.484 --> 00:42:45.111
About?

00:42:45.153 --> 00:42:47.087
Oh, it's nothing
really important.

00:42:47.121 --> 00:42:49.954
Just your basic Borg-human
cultural differences.

00:42:49.991 --> 00:42:51.891
Really?

00:42:51.926 --> 00:42:53.917
That's not what she says.

00:42:53.962 --> 00:42:55.987
You...

00:42:56.097 --> 00:42:56.995
Y-You...

00:42:57.098 --> 00:42:58.929
You spoke...
You spoke to her.

00:42:58.967 --> 00:43:01.765
She seems to think
you're making good progress.

00:43:01.803 --> 00:43:03.828
She finds you
reasonably efficient,

00:43:03.872 --> 00:43:06.432
and says you've been
helping her learn more

00:43:06.474 --> 00:43:08.738
about our complex
social interactions.

00:43:08.776 --> 00:43:10.767
Any idea what she meant by that?

00:43:10.812 --> 00:43:13.906
I can't imagine.

00:43:13.948 --> 00:43:15.813
You two make a good team.

00:43:15.850 --> 00:43:19.115
I want to keep you together
on this project.

00:43:19.153 --> 00:43:20.586
Sir...

00:43:22.190 --> 00:43:23.555
Aye, sir.

00:43:23.591 --> 00:43:25.786
And maybe others in the future.

00:43:25.827 --> 00:43:27.522
Have fun.

00:43:34.035 --> 00:43:35.434
I've stopped
the internal bleeding

00:43:35.470 --> 00:43:37.097
and repaired the tissue damage.

00:43:37.138 --> 00:43:40.335
Your pericardium is
clean as a whistle.

00:43:40.375 --> 00:43:43.310
Which is more than I can say
for my Sick Bay.

00:43:43.344 --> 00:43:44.333
I'm sorry about the mess.

00:43:44.379 --> 00:43:47.542
I haven't had time to clean up.

00:43:47.582 --> 00:43:48.913
It was a hectic day.

00:43:48.950 --> 00:43:50.713
I treated two broken bones,

00:43:50.752 --> 00:43:53.346
an upset stomach
and a lacerated hand.

00:43:53.388 --> 00:43:56.118
Does this mean you're too tired
to meet later...

00:43:56.157 --> 00:43:58.182
in my quarters?

00:43:58.226 --> 00:44:00.160
Are you sure
your heart can take it?

00:44:00.194 --> 00:44:02.719
I'm detecting
elevated hormonal levels.

00:44:02.764 --> 00:44:04.527
If you two don't take it easy,

00:44:04.565 --> 00:44:07.056
I'll have to declare
a medical emergency.

00:44:07.101 --> 00:44:10.195
If you'll excuse me,
I have to go check on Harry.

00:44:10.238 --> 00:44:12.672
I hear he's having
a nervous breakdown.

00:44:12.707 --> 00:44:13.935
It's a long story.

00:44:14.042 --> 00:44:15.339
Not so fast, Mr. Paris.

00:44:15.376 --> 00:44:17.401
You are going
to help me sterilize

00:44:17.445 --> 00:44:19.879
every square millimeter
of this Sick Bay.

00:44:19.914 --> 00:44:23.350
No doubt, you've left your oily
residue on every hypospray,

00:44:23.384 --> 00:44:26.410
your sloughed secretions
on every console.

00:44:27.522 --> 00:44:28.955
Just kidding.

00:44:29.057 --> 00:44:30.684
In fact,
I've had a change of heart

00:44:30.725 --> 00:44:32.556
about my fastidiousness.

00:44:32.593 --> 00:44:35.255
A little clutter
never hurt anyone.

00:44:35.296 --> 00:44:38.561
Sick Bay should have a more
organic touch, don't you think?

00:44:38.599 --> 00:44:41.329
To help our patients feel...
more at home?

00:44:48.142 --> 00:44:50.804
What's gotten into him?

00:44:50.845 --> 00:44:53.006
It's a long story.
